{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue\/start","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"start","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"case","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL23MXLStartStopDiscontinueO5startyA2CmF","title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue.start"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue\/start"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The start of an ending, typically associated with the left barline of the first measure.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"start","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopDiscontinue":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue","title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The start-stop-discontinue type is used to specify ending types. Typically, the start type is associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a downward","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is typical for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second endings that do not conclude a piece."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopDiscontinue/start":{"title":"MXLStartStopDiscontinue.start","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopdiscontinue\/start","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopDiscontinue\/start","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"start"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The start of an ending, typically associated with the left barline of the first measure.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"}}}